\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 On 23 October one address from Rostelecom in Russia hit the fake SSH server on my Azure sensor. Between 07:32 and 19:57 UTC it made 28,724 connections, and every one was a failed login as root, nearly always with a different password. That is 143,622 events, about one in nine of everything I logged. None of the logins worked. It is a plain password-guessing attack. GreyNoise tags it as an SSH bruteforcer and AbuseIPDB scores it 88%, but SANS gave it a 0. It gained nothing, because the honeypot is fake, and it lost its cover.\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

